{'title': {'value': 'Conditional Sampling of Variational Autoencoders via Iterated Approximate Ancestral Sampling'}, 'abstract': {'value': 'Conditional sampling of variational autoencoders (VAEs) is needed in various applications, such as missing data imputation, but is computationally intractable. A principled choice for asymptotically exact conditional sampling is Metropolis-within-Gibbs (MWG). However, we observe that the tendency of VAEs to learn a structured latent space, a commonly desired property, can cause the MWG sampler to get “stuck” far from the target distribution. This paper mitigates the limitations of MWG: we systematically outline the pitfalls in the context of VAEs, propose two original methods that address these pitfalls, and demonstrate an improved performance of the proposed methods on a set of sampling tasks.'}, 'authors': {'value': ['Vaidotas Simkus', 'Michael U. Gutmann']}, 'authorids': {'value': ['~Vaidotas_Simkus1', '~Michael_U._Gutmann1']}, 'pdf': {'value': '/pdf/db64390828e9dc6d5b8ce9c3f681827c7a77f95f.pdf'}, 'submission_length': {'value': 'Regular submission (no more than 12 pages of main content)'}, 'venue': {'value': 'Accepted by TMLR'}, 'venueid': {'value': 'TMLR'}, '_bibtex': {'value': '@article{
