year={2023},
url={https://openreview.net/forum?id=HVAeM6sNo8},
note={}
}"}, 'assigned_action_editor': {'value': '~Nicolas_THOME2'}, 'changes_since_last_submission': {'value': "- Methodology, Introduction and Result sections have been revised per reviewer's comments. 
- Two extra tables were added to the manuscript per reviewer's comments.
- Figure 1 and Figure 2 were modified per reviewer's comments.
- More details added to the Discussion section per reviewer's comments."}, 'video': {'value': 'https://drive.google.com/file/d/1AXjAHw2Ef3Ni_uqZpoih9r72Jq-nHc5F/view?usp=sharing'}, 'license': {'value': 'Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)'}, 'paperhash': {'value': 'dadsetan|robust_alzheimers_progression_modeling_using_crossdomain_selfsupervised_deep_learning'}}

{'title': {'value': 'Denise: Deep Robust Principal Component Analysis for Positive Semidefinite Matrices'}, 'abstract': {'value': 'The robust PCA of covariance matrices plays an essential role when isolating key explanatory features.  The currently available methods for performing such a low-rank plus sparse decomposition are matrix specific, meaning, those algorithms must re-run for every new matrix.  Since these algorithms are computationally expensive, it is preferable to learn and store a function that nearly instantaneously performs this decomposition when evaluated.  Therefore, we introduce Denise, a deep learning-based algorithm for robust PCA of covariance matrices, or more generally, of symmetric positive semidefinite matrices, which learns precisely such a function.  Theoretical guarantees for Denise are provided.  These include a novel universal approximation theorem adapted to our geometric deep learning problem and convergence to an optimal solution to the learning problem.  Our experiments show that Denise matches state-of-the-art performance in terms of decomposition quality, while being approximately $2000\times$ faster than the state-of-the-art, principal component pursuit (PCP), and $200 \times$ faster than the current speed-optimized method, fast PCP. '}, 'authors': {'value': ['Calypso Herrera', 'Florian Krach', 'Anastasis Kratsios', 'Pierre Ruyssen', 'Josef Teichmann']}, 'authorids': {'value': ['~Calypso_Herrera1', '~Florian_Krach1', '~Anastasis_Kratsios1', '~Pierre_Ruyssen1', '~Josef_Teichmann2']}, 'pdf': {'value': '/pdf/7277d06692f207735f641e422d69eca11ca19d19.pdf'}, 'submission_length': {'value': 'Long submission (more than 12 pages of main content)'}, 'previous_TMLR_submission_url': {'value': 'https://openreview.net/forum?id=1JJmOkEmlB'}, 'changes_since_last_submission': {'value': 'We want to thank the referees and the action editor for their helpful feedback and for reviewing our manuscript in detail.  We very much appreciate your hard work and the quality of the reviews, and we believe it really helped improve the quality of our submission.

Thanks a lot,

The authors.'}, 'venue': {'value': 'Accepted by TMLR'}, 'venueid': {'value': 'TMLR'}, '_bibtex': {'value': '@article{
herrera2023denise,
