url={https://openreview.net/forum?id=MTFf1rDDEI},
note={}
}'}, 'assigned_action_editor': {'value': '~Marcello_Restelli1'}, 'changes_since_last_submission': {'value': ' - updated Figure 2 a by depicting the agent the features
 - added acknowledgments on page 11
 - modified equations 16 and 41 to contain the indicator function, instead of two cases, for the observed feature and the unobserved features
 - minor updates to proofs and explanations according to the comments of the third reviewer (see https://openreview.net/forum?id=MTFf1rDDEI&noteId=ELzMKfMCPa for details)'}, 'video': {'value': 'https://youtu.be/RYemlh2NSzQ'}, 'code': {'value': 'https://gitlab.inria.fr/robotlearn/sfr_learning'}, 'certifications': {'value': []}, 'license': {'value': 'Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)'}, 'paperhash': {'value': 'reinke|successor_feature_representations'}}

{'title': {'value': 'A Kernel Perspective on Behavioural Metrics for Markov Decision Processes'}, 'abstract': {'value': 'We present a novel perspective on behavioural metrics for Markov decision processes via the use of positive definite kernels. We define a new metric under this lens that is provably equivalent to the recently introduced MICo distance (Castro et al., 2021). The kernel perspective enables us to provide new theoretical results, including value-function bounds and low-distortion finite-dimensional Euclidean embeddings, which are crucial when using behavioural metrics for reinforcement learning representations. We complement our theory with strong empirical results that demonstrate the effectiveness of these methods in practice.'}, 'authors': {'value': ['Pablo Samuel Castro', 'Tyler Kastner', 'Prakash Panangaden', 'Mark Rowland']}, 'authorids': {'value': ['~Pablo_Samuel_Castro1', '~Tyler_Kastner1', '~Prakash_Panangaden1', '~Mark_Rowland1']}, 'pdf': {'value': '/pdf/bd29c539d2a379cef0b7afefddd67067d148feb7.pdf'}, 'submission_length': {'value': 'Long submission (more than 12 pages of main content)'}, 'supplementary_material': {'value': '/attachment/3efce3a5b936451421a8617914636ceb6e320f8f.zip'}, 'venue': {'value': 'Accepted by TMLR'}, 'venueid': {'value': 'TMLR'}, '_bibtex': {'value': '@article{
