{'title': {'value': 'Generalization bounds for Kernel Canonical Correlation Analysis'}, 'abstract': {'value': 'We study the problem of multiview representation learning using kernel canonical correlation analysis (KCCA) and establish non-asymptotic bounds on generalization error for regularized empirical risk minimization. In particular, we give fine-grained high-probability bounds on generalization error ranging from $O(n^{-1/6})$  to $O(n^{-1/5})$ depending on underlying distributional properties, where $n$ is the number of data samples. For the special case of finite-dimensional Hilbert spaces (such as linear CCA), our rates improve, ranging from $O(n^{-1/2})$ to $O(n^{-1})$. Finally, our results generalize to the problem of functional canonical correlation analysis over abstract Hilbert spaces.'}, 'authors': {'value': ['Enayat Ullah', 'Raman Arora'], 'readers': ['everyone']}, 'authorids': {'value': ['~Enayat_Ullah1', '~Raman_Arora1'], 'readers': ['everyone']}, 'pdf': {'value': '/pdf/8459b7993e2f29566ad8e13d5f7f224cf496de28.pdf'}, 'submission_length': {'value': 'Regular submission (no more than 12 pages of main content)'}, 'venue': {'value': 'Accepted by TMLR'}, 'venueid': {'value': 'TMLR'}, '_bibtex': {'value': '@article{
